.TH GDRIVE-UPLOAD 1 "October 2026" "scripts" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gdrive-upload \- quick direct upload of files and folders to Google Drive via Rclone
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gdrive-upload
[\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
[\fIFILE\fR|\fIDIR\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBgdrive-upload\fR uploads specified files or directories directly to the configured Google Drive destination
(default: \fBgdrive_dev:Synced\fR) using \fBrclone copy\fR or \fBrclone copyto\fR without requiring a full bidirectional sync.
.PP
If the target files or directories are located within the synchronization root (\fB$HOME/Remote/Synced\fR),
the script strips the root prefix and preserves the relative directory hierarchy on the remote storage.
.PP
This utility functions as both a standalone command-line tool and an integration backend for GNOME Nautilus
context menu actions (\fBCopy Selected to Google Drive\fR).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Displays brief command-line help and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SYNC_SUBVOL
Local root synchronization directory (default: \fB$HOME/Remote/Synced\fR).
.TP
.B SYNC_REMOTE
Rclone remote destination (default: \fBgdrive_dev:Synced\fR).
.TP
.B SYNC_QUICK_LOG
Log file destination (default: \fB/tmp/rclone_quick_upload.log\fR).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rclone (1),
.BR bisync-synced (1),
.BR scripts (1)
